{
  "report": {
    "kind": "report",
    "slug": "customer-growth",
    "id": "obj_01m68056y0p6wrtatxp5cq0dgd",
    "project": "prj_01m680560xk3swdyev8hcftkgy",
    "title": "Customer growth",
    "description": "How the customer base grew, where customers are, and who they are.",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "since",
        "type": "date",
        "default": "2020-01-01",
        "label": "Since"
      }
    ],
    "queries": {
      "kpis": {
        "sql": "WITH m AS (\n  SELECT date_trunc('month', subscription_date) AS month, count(*) AS signups\n  FROM customers\n  WHERE subscription_date >= $since\n  GROUP BY 1\n),\nt AS (\n  SELECT count(*) AS customers, count(DISTINCT country) AS countries\n  FROM customers\n  WHERE subscription_date >= $since\n)\nSELECT t.customers,\n       t.countries,\n       (SELECT round(avg(signups)) FROM m) AS avg_monthly_signups,\n       (SELECT strftime(month, '%B %Y') FROM m ORDER BY signups DESC, month LIMIT 1) AS peak_month,\n       (SELECT max(signups) FROM m) AS peak_month_signups\nFROM t\n"
      },
      "monthly": {
        "sql": "WITH m AS (\n  SELECT CAST(date_trunc('month', subscription_date) AS DATE) AS month, count(*) AS signups\n  FROM customers\n  WHERE subscription_date >= $since\n  GROUP BY 1\n),\nx AS (SELECT month, signups, (month - DATE '2000-01-01') AS d FROM m)\nSELECT month,\n       signups,\n       round(regr_intercept(signups, d) OVER () + regr_slope(signups, d) OVER () * d) AS trend\nFROM x\nORDER BY month\n"
      },
      "top_countries": {
        "sql": "SELECT country,\n       count(*) AS customers,\n       round(100.0 * count(*) / sum(count(*)) OVER (), 2) AS share_pct,\n       round(100.0 * sum(count(*)) OVER (ORDER BY count(*) DESC, country) / sum(count(*)) OVER (), 2) AS cumulative_pct\nFROM customers\nWHERE subscription_date >= $since\nGROUP BY 1\nORDER BY customers DESC, country\nLIMIT 15\n"
      },
      "weekday_month": {
        "sql": "SELECT month(subscription_date) AS month_num,\n       strftime(subscription_date, '%b') AS month,\n       isodow(subscription_date) AS dow_num,\n       strftime(subscription_date, '%a') AS weekday,\n       round(count(*) * 1.0 / count(DISTINCT subscription_date), 1) AS avg_signups_per_day,\n       count(*) AS signups\nFROM customers\nWHERE subscription_date >= $since\nGROUP BY 1, 2, 3, 4\nORDER BY 1, 3\n"
      },
      "email_tld": {
        "sql": "WITH t AS (\n  SELECT split_part(split_part(email, '@', 2), '.', -1) AS tld, count(*) AS customers\n  FROM customers\n  WHERE subscription_date >= $since\n  GROUP BY 1\n),\nr AS (SELECT tld, customers, row_number() OVER (ORDER BY customers DESC, tld) AS rk FROM t)\nSELECT CASE WHEN rk <= 8 THEN tld ELSE 'Other' END AS tld,\n       sum(customers) AS customers,\n       min(CASE WHEN rk <= 8 THEN rk ELSE 9 END) AS slice_order\nFROM r\nGROUP BY 1\nORDER BY slice_order\n"
      },
      "legal_form": {
        "sql": "SELECT CASE\n         WHEN company LIKE '% LLC' THEN 'LLC'\n         WHEN company LIKE '% Ltd' THEN 'Ltd'\n         WHEN company LIKE '% PLC' THEN 'PLC'\n         WHEN company LIKE '% Inc' THEN 'Inc'\n         WHEN company LIKE '% and Sons' THEN 'and Sons'\n         WHEN company LIKE '% Group' THEN 'Group'\n         ELSE 'Other'\n       END AS legal_form,\n       count(*) AS customers\nFROM customers\nWHERE subscription_date >= $since\nGROUP BY 1\nORDER BY customers DESC\n"
      }
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "text": "## Customer growth\n\nA look at the 500,000-customer CRM sample: how many people signed up each\nmonth, where they live, what their email addresses and company names look\nlike. Use the **Since** filter to restrict everything to sign-ups on or\nafter a date.\n"
